{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"864","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Fair Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya and Vasya decided to play a game. They have "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an even number). A single integer is written on each card."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Before the game Petya will choose an integer and after that Vasya will choose another integer ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the number that Petya chose). During the game each player takes all the cards with number he chose. For example, if Petya chose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" before the game he will take all cards on which "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" is written and if Vasya chose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" before the game he will take all cards on which "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" is written."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The game is considered fair if Petya and Vasya can take all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards, and the number of cards each player gets is the same."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine whether Petya and Vasya can choose integer numbers before the game so that the game is fair. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":") — number of cards. It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an even number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain a sequence of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" (one integer per line, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":") — numbers written on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible for Petya and Vasya to choose numbers in such a way that the game will be fair, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) in the first line. In this case you should not print anything more."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the other case print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) in the first line. In the second line print two distinct integers — number that Petya should choose and the number that Vasya should choose to make the game fair. If there are several solutions, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n11\n27\n27\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n11 27\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n6\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n10\n20\n30\n20\n10\n20\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n1\n1\n2\n2\n3\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example the game will be fair if, for example, Petya chooses number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"11"},{"kind":"text","text":", and Vasya chooses number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"27"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the will take all cards — Petya will take cards "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", and Vasya will take cards "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, each of them will take exactly two cards."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example fair game is impossible because the numbers written on the cards are equal, but the numbers that Petya and Vasya should choose should be distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example it is impossible to take all cards. Petya and Vasya can take at most five cards — for example, Petya can choose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" and Vasya can choose number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"20"},{"kind":"text","text":". But for the game to be fair it is necessary to take "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"6"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"864A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/864/problem/A"}